            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Chay Zenhouse",
            "review_text": "PhongTiuuu\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam9 contributions\n0\nChill\nNov 2023 • Solo\nIn the heart of Saigon, hidden in a small alley, where there are no car horns, a place that makes our hearts choke with its peaceful space. The swing, the small bridge, the swinging wind chimes and the sparkling lights behind the rows of leaves. Just simple, rustic things that have kept a fastidious diner like me from eating salty food for 3 years. Switched to vegetarian because I fell in love with the space and food here.\n• I still clearly remember the first time I set foot here because of a friend's introduction. As soon as I set foot in, there was a wide open space with many trees, flowers, leaves and many kind people who like silence and privacy. I find peace and quiet after hours of hard work.\n• The dishes and drinks are delicious and eye-catching and have a variety of Asian and European genres for you to choose from to eat mango without getting bored of Asia.\nIf you are in Saigon, please try to come and experience to see if what I share is true. Sometimes it's even more than that. A hi. Have a good day\nRead more\nShow original\nWritten November 10, 2023",
