            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Chay Zenhouse",
            "review_text": "xuân vũ\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam3 contributions\n2\nRight zenhouse, right time\nOct 2023 • Solo\n- \"I resign...\"\nWalking aimlessly in the middle of people and busy cars after shouting in the middle of the office like that. Now, both my body and soul feel tired and bored. Right now I just need a quiet place and something a little warm. I need to \"slow down\" and separate myself from the hustle and bustle of life.\nSuddenly, an alley covered with yellow and red lanterns seemed to awaken my heart. My gut feeling tells me that maybe this is the place I'm looking for.\nA cool space, melodious music and a flock of koi fish swimming around under the magical yellow light brought me back to the tranquility of my soul.\nZen House, here I feel open to nature, open to myself. Even though I don't want to eat anything right now, I opened the menu just to show off. Looking at a few dishes, it was as if there was some kind of magic on each page that stimulated my taste buds. I ordered a few dishes to enjoy the so-called \"pure green culinary value\".\nI chose for myself a quite chill corner next to the southern island with the sound of gurgling water from a teapot covered with cool green moss. Here you can see the entire restaurant. The shop's campus is very spacious and airy, divided into many very reasonable areas. If you want to be in harmony with nature, choose the area like I chose, and if you want a private space, you can choose the VIP room area. There are even Japanese-style sitting rooms or meeting and party rooms... I think if there was an infinity pool, it would be no different from a 5-star resort.\nWhile letting my soul soar above the treetops, the aroma of bowls of noodle soup, plates of baked Japanese mushrooms covered with golden cheese,... pulled me back to the ground. I devoured everything on the table because it was truly delicious, and I knew that to create great dishes like this, the owner of this restaurant and his staff had to know nothing. How much effort goes into this.\nPerhaps seeing me sitting alone seemed a bit sad, so the manager came to talk to me. Through him, I also learned that the restaurant also has many volunteer music shows performed by blind people on special days and occasions that are very interesting and meaningful. Hopefully I will have the opportunity to participate. He also said that Ms. Zen (the familiar name everyone calls her), the restaurant's owner, is also a philanthropist and a sponsor. She often sponsors and helps orphaned children. Many times I wonder where human value lies? Through my sister's actions, I can realize that my value lies in how many people I can help and how many people I can save, but not in houses, cars or phones. phone...\nGot it, I'm full, I'm relieved... Thank you Zen House.\nZen House, rekindles desires.\nRead more\nShow original\nWritten October 21, 2023",
